He ran forth surrounded by six hundred crores of gaṇas. / And Śaṅkukarṇa, of great strength, approached with a crore of gaṇas; / and Nandika with ten [crores], and Piṅgākṣa with eight;
Vināyaka, renowned by the name Kuṣmāṇḍa, with sixty-four [crores];
Hiraṇyavarṇa with six, and Ekapād likewise; / Dhūmrakeśa with twelve, and Patākī with ten;
Sahasraghaṇṭa with eighteen, and Tapas with five; / Sahasraśīrṣa with six, and Bhava surrounded by a crore;
Vara arrived with ten, and Kumbhakarṇa with eight; / Viṣvaksena with a thousand, and Anada with a hundred;
Āveśana likewise with eight, and Pravartana with seven; / Mahārava, leader of gaṇas, surrounded by a thousand gaṇas; / Caturmukha with twelve, and Bāhuprahāraka; / Mahākāla with a hundred, and the gaṇa Agniśikhara;

Ādityamūrdhan with a crore, and Dhanāvaha likewise; / Sannābha with a hundred, and Kukkuṭa with eight;
